  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Independent, representative, effective and sustainable employer and business membership organizations have a critical role to play in labour market governance. This biennium the ILO has continued to support the Vanuatu Chamber of Commerce and Industry (VCCI) strengthen its institutional and organizational capacities. Notable initiatives have included training on good governance, leadership and advocacy for the executive council and committee members of the Chamber; training of sectretariat staff to deliver training on women&apos;s empowerment targeting women managers;  collaboration on sectoral research into skills needs in the construction and tourism sectors and associated policy workshops; and technical assistance and support for the Chamber to launch the &quot;Worker Ready, Investment Ready&quot; programme providing targeted training and coaching to seasonal workers and their families at the start of the labour mobility cycle. The &quot;Worker Ready, Investment Ready&quot; program is facilitated through collaboration with the Department of Labour (DOL) and the Department of Rural Development and Agriculture (DARD).</narrative>
  </description>
